## Merge coherence (the note I was told to verify, not assume)

`80abbcc` does not touch `internal/models/transaction.go` at all
(`git show --name-only 80abbcc | grep -c internal/models/transaction.go` -> 0),
confirming A5's version was dropped and A3's kept.

I then diffed A5's dropped version against the merged A3 version:

    diff -u <repo>/internal/models/transaction.go /tmp/swarm-worktrees/budget2/work/A5/internal/models/transaction.go

The differences are entirely comments and field ordering. Semantically the two
are IDENTICAL where A5 depends on them:
  - `Income = "Income"`, `Outflow = "Outflow"`, `Transfer = "Transfer"` — same
    constant values in both.
  - `TransferClass string \`json:"transfer_class,omitempty"\`` — same name, type,
    tag; both documents define the values as "paired" / "external" / "".
  - `TransferPairKey string \`json:"transfer_pair_key,omitempty"\`` — same.

A5's own dropped comment even says: 'A5's projection reads it to identify
confirmed inbound paired transfers as a reference amount' — the same contract
A3's version provides. No A5 behavior depended on a differing definition. The
merged tree compiles (`go build ./...` rc=0) and the package's tests pass, so
`projection.go` genuinely compiles and runs against A3's definitions.

